<!--Post: 4227--><!--Time: 1105913414-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4227"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 16, 2005 - 2:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read on the BTK crime library story that BTK <BR>told Kevin that he was wanted in California by the police . Think the is true?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4227-->
<!--Post: 4252--><!--Time: 1105973580-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4252"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 17, 2005 - 6:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If this is a BTK crime, which I am pretty sure it is, then I doubt it. Because he said he was wanted in California, wanted to steal their car to go to New York. Obviously he didn&#39;t go to New York. I think he said that to try to keep the situation calm until got them tied up so he could do what he set out to do.  <BR> <BR>It may be because I&#39;m from a big city, &#40;which Wichita very well might be, I don&#39;t know&#41; but if someone was in my house telling me that they were wanted in one specific place, and was planning to go to another specific place, a red flag would be raised in my mind to run and scream. Why would he tell a victim where to find him unless he was going to kill them?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4252-->
<!--Post: 5006--><!--Time: 1106848982-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5006"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 10:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kevin also said he tied up his sister and he broke loose...so were the knots Kevin tied the same as the Otero&#39;s?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5006-->
<!--Post: 7053--><!--Time: 1108153448-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7053"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 12:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kevin says that the killer told them he was from California and needed a car. Then he asks Kevin &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the University?&#34; <BR> <BR>Of course, the first statement could have been made just to keep them calm and thinking they were in no danger if they didn&#39;t resist. <BR> <BR>My question would be: At what point was Kevin asked about the University? Does anyone know? <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7053-->
<!--Post: 7080--><!--Time: 1108173387-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7080"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 5:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I recall reading in an article that BTK told Kevin Bright he was wanted in California...the cops were after him there.  I also recall that BTK asked Kevin Bright &#34;Haven&#39;t I seen you at the University?&#34;.. <BR>I suppose BTK gave Bright this information as he was busily KNOWING Kevin Bright was going to die that day...but ...as it turns out, Kevin lived to tell us that BTK asked him about the University...and letting Bright know the cops in CA were after him.... <BR> <BR>I find both of those mentions by BTK very interesting...thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7080-->
<!--Post: 7092--><!--Time: 1108178168-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7092"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 7:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m with Beck.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7092-->
<!--Post: 7114--><!--Time: 1108188296-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7114"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 10:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is not unlike the Zodiac Killer at Lake Berryessa, where he told his victims that he was an escaped convict from Deer Lodge, Montana, and that he killed a guard and stole a car, and needed another one to get to Mexico.  He expected both Bryan Hartnell and Cecelia Shepard to die, and yet made up a story &#40;subsequent inquiries indicated that there were no recent escapees&#41;; Hartnell survived and related what was said.  BTK obviously studied the Zodiac case and mimicked the Lake Berryessa attack to a certain extent with the Brights.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7114-->
<!--Post: 7175--><!--Time: 1108258321-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7175"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 5:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Binding robbery victims in their house happens every day. Charles Manson himself bound one or both of the LaBiancas&#39; and told them they were going to be robbed. Bugliosi didn&#39;t use any quotes but apparently Manson successfully completed his task, telling the LaBiacas to be calm, they only wanted to rob them. <BR> <BR>Kevin Bright took gunshots to the head and was interviewed thirty years later. I think the information in his interview needs to be analyzed with this in mind. <BR> <BR>I guess my point is that I don&#39;t find a lot here to get excited about, although I don&#39;t entirely dismiss it, either. A robber - in this case, a murderer - needs to say something when he&#39;s talking to his victims. I don&#39;t think the California mention is significant. What I do find significant is the need to say he was wanted by police. This makes him sound tough, more dangerous and would get the victims to comply at a faster rate, in my opinion. <BR> <BR>Ed, didn&#39;t Ranger White first say &#34;Colorado?&#34; I know Colorado was dismissed and Hartnell then half-heartedly agreed that Z had said, &#34;Deer Lodge, MT.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7175-->
<!--Post: 7293--><!--Time: 1108371981-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7293"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 1:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.whoownsjackkerouac.com/wayne2.html" target=_top>http://www.whoownsjackkerouac.com/wayne2.html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.whoownsjackkerouac.com/people2b.html" target=_top>http://www.whoownsjackkerouac.com/people2b.html</a> <BR>Larry and Amy <BR> <BR><a href="http://al.gcsu.edu/dlow4.htm" target=_top>http://al.gcsu.edu/dlow4.htm</a> <BR><a href="http://old.lawrence.com/burroughs/wsb_photo1.html" target=_top>http://old.lawrence.com/burroughs/wsb_photo1.html</a> <BR><a href="http://old.lawrence.com/burroughs/wsb_photo4.html" target=_top>http://old.lawrence.com/burroughs/wsb_photo4.html</a> <BR><a href="http://www.ardmoreite.com/stories/080397/news/news08.html" target=_top>http://www.ardmoreite.com/stories/080397/news/news 08.html</a> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.wuacc.edu/reference/cks/lists/kslitinprint.html" target=_top>http://www.wuacc.edu/reference/cks/lists/kslitinpr int.html</a> <BR>Propst, Wayne &#40;Lawrence&#41;. Endocrine Systems. Cottonwood Press, Box J, Kansas Union, University of Kansas, Lawrence, KS 66045 &#40;913-864- 3777&#41;, 1988. $2.00.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7293-->
<!--Post: 12094--><!--Time: 1111565844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12094"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 12:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is from Skov via e-mail: <BR> <BR> <BR> Kevin B and changing description of BTK   <BR>  <BR>Take a look at this picture: <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.raderlodge.com/pg3_3.html" target=_top>http://www.raderlodge.com/pg3_3.html</a>  <BR> <BR>Interesting to look at the cloths the guy to the left is wearing! <BR> <BR>Think about the description that Kevin Brights brother gave of what BTK was wearing. <BR> <BR>first he said orage shirt or jacket <BR> <BR>then he changed it to camoflge jacket!!! <BR> <BR>This guy to the left in the pic &#40;and other hunters&#41; wear both! <BR> <BR>And this picture is even from the RADER LOGE website in Kansas. <BR> <BR>SO! did BTK wear his hunter outfit the day he killed Kathryn and tryed to kill her brother Kevin as well, and did the Bright brother change his description because BTK was wearing both a camulfage jacket AND a orange  <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12094-->
<!--Post: 12095--><!--Time: 1111567135-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12095"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 12:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To be wearing both and not looking out of place it would probably need to be during a hunting season and I think the closest hunting season in Kansas to the Bright murder is turkey hunting but that isn&#39;t until the second week in April and the Bright murder was April 4th.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12095-->
<!--Post: 12103--><!--Time: 1111584167-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12103"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 5:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think Kevin may have said a hunting jacket, and since he was shot, the cops arent going to spend hours interrogating him. Brief despcription, he said hunting jacket, the cops took that to mean an orange jacket, and ran with it. What Kev meant was camoflage jacket. just my opin.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12103-->
